 "circuits": [],
 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Internal arrangement",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Four diodes form a full bridge. Each AC lead joins the anode of one diode and the cathode of another; the two free cathodes meet at +, the two free anodes at -. The leads run -, ~, ~, + along one edge of the case."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Polarity",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The lead polarity is marked on the front of the case, and the + lead is the one beside the bevelled corner."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current derating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Bolted to a heatsink, the bridge carries the full 8.0 A up to a case temperature of about 62 °C, falling in a straight line to zero at 150 °C. Mounted on a PCB with 12 mm square pads and 9.5 mm leads, it carries about 3.9 A up to an ambient of about 47 °C, falling in a straight line to zero at 150 °C. Both lines hold for a 60 Hz load, resistive or inductive."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Surge",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "IFSM is 200 A for a single sine-wave on rated load. Taken at TJ = 150 °C with 8.3 ms half sine-waves, the allowed peak per diode falls with the number of 60 Hz cycles, to about 108 A at 10 cycles and about 70 A at 100."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Mounting",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The case has a slotted mounting hole through its body. Mounting torque is 10 cm-kg (8.8 inch-lb) at most, and 5.7 cm-kg (5 inch-lb) is the recommended figure. RθJC is with the case on an aluminium plate heatsink; the recommended mounting is bolted down to a heatsink with #6 screws and silicone thermal compound between them."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction and soldering",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The moulding compound is rated UL 94 V-0. Leads are matte tin plated, solderable to J-STD-002 and JESD 22-B102, and the E3 and M3 versions pass the JESD 201 class 1A whisker test. The leads take a solder dip of up to 275 °C for 10 s, per JESD 22-B106. E3 parts are RoHS-compliant; M3 parts are also halogen-free."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Full-wave rectification of mains AC to DC in power supplies, switch-mode supplies and adapters, monitors, TVs, printers, audio gear and household appliances."
  }
 ],
